from pathlib import Path
import json,html,re
from analyze import NAMES
ROOT=Path(__file__).resolve().parent
s=json.loads((ROOT/'analysis/summary.json').read_text());p=s['policies'];ex=json.loads((ROOT/'data/execution.json').read_text())
md=[];ht=[]
def inline(t):
    t=html.escape(str(t));t=re.sub(r'\[([^]]+)\]\(([^)]+)\)',r'<a href="\2">\1</a>',t)
    t=re.sub(r'\*\*([^*]+)\*\*',r'<strong>\1</strong>',t)
    t=re.sub(r'(?<!\*)\*([^*]+)\*(?!\*)',r'<em>\1</em>',t)
    return re.sub(r'`([^`]+)`',r'<code>\1</code>',t)
def h(t,n=2):md.append('#'*n+' '+t);ht.append(f'<h{n}>{inline(t)}</h{n}>')
def para(t):md.append(t);ht.append('<p>'+inline(t)+'</p>')
def table(headers,rows):
    md.append('\n'.join(['| '+' | '.join(headers)+' |','| '+' | '.join(['---']*len(headers))+' |']+['| '+' | '.join(map(str,r))+' |' for r in rows]))
    ht.append('<div class="scroll"><table><thead><tr>'+''.join('<th>'+inline(x)+'</th>' for x in headers)+'</tr></thead><tbody>'+''.join('<tr>'+''.join('<td>'+inline(x)+'</td>' for x in r)+'</tr>' for r in rows)+'</tbody></table></div>')
def fig(name,caption):md.extend([f'![{caption}](analysis/{name}.png)',caption]);ht.append(f'<figure><img src="analysis/{name}.png" alt="{html.escape(caption)}"><figcaption>{inline(caption)}</figcaption></figure>')
def code(t):md.append('```sh\n'+t+'\n```');ht.append('<pre>'+html.escape(t)+'</pre>')
def percent(policy,metric='mean_needs_met'):return 100*p[policy][metric]['mean']
h('One person and a moving idea',1)
para('Streams and Rocks • current interpretation updated 22 October 2026 • historical community benchmarks retained below')
para('**Smoke is inward speaking, Clay is inward listening, and the middle is the idea moving between them within one person’s two-in-one. Wind, Fog, Water and Mist describe the moving idea itself.** Water represents perceived balance. The author now gives D₂O the role of a small compositional change with potentially large consequences, including a change from life-saving to potentially life-threatening. Its effect must be specified and observed; the name alone does not determine help or harm. Every person has their own history.')
para('The [new history and form tests](../community-two-in-one-application/README.md) add a person-specific runner for the unchanged corpus component equations, 48 coupled synthetic trials, and an audit of 840 real thought probes from 24 people. Different input orders leave different fields even at the same final accumulator, while exchanging only Smoke/Clay labels changes nothing because the equations do not use those labels. Fourteen unit tests, 89 original saved checks and 69 additional Miro-derived numerical checks pass. The full empirical two-in-one application remains unfinished: these records do not separately measure the inward functions, meaning, history contents or idea forms. No simpler predictor is substituted.')
para('The [updated corpus and live Miro review](../community-two-in-one-application/MIRO_CONNECTIONS.md) traces meaning, expression, context, memory and threshold tests to three relevant boards. The available corrected DOCX matches the source used in the latest runs. Mirroring the full signed field and source history leaves movement unchanged, showing why movement alone cannot identify every internal distinction. The board’s proposed forgetting rules remain explicit alternatives; no decay was silently added to the exact corpus dynamics.')
para('The [exact corpus equations and new data audit](../community-two-in-one-field/README.md) retain the full coupled field dynamics. Eighteen numerical trials, 12 unit tests and 272 saved-result checks pass. The new public source contains 6,434 annotated thoughts from 118 people. A full empirical two-in-one fit remains unresolved: the inward roles, utility and idea forms still need their observation links to the corpus variables. No simpler predictor was substituted in this study.')
para('The ideas came first and were translated into the Navier–Stokes format. The [inverse translation](../community-two-in-one-field/INVERSE_TRANSLATION.md) now works backward: accumulated influence changes context, movement carries context, and context differences can redirect movement. Smoke and Clay are proposed putting-forward and receiving functions within that loop. The reconstruction identifies what the equations retain, what their fluid assumptions add, and what they do not separately record about memory contents, felt time or perceived balance. This changes the interpretation and testing specification, not the saved results.')
para('The [earlier testing document and public-data probes](../community-two-in-one/README.md) include an editable protocol and episode/history forms. A separate statistical comparator using past questionnaire answers predicts later reported inner dialogue with error 0.2134 versus 0.2567 for a population estimate. Older memories contain more counted content in 31.25% of within-person older/newer comparisons on average. These earlier findings do not fit or validate the full inner field.')
para('Read the [current roles](SITUATIONAL_ROLES.md), [connections and evidence](CONNECTIONS.md), and [editable testing document](../community-two-in-one/Two_in_one_testing_protocol.docx). The seven-person allocation and earlier external-dialogue studies below concern separate questions; their numerical results remain unchanged.')
h('Historical studies of community and external encounters')
para('The original allocation benchmark used seven fictional participants and explicit synthetic rules inspired by the uploaded Foucault passage. [How the passage was used](interpretation.md) · [Methods and units](methods.md) · [Source provenance](source_provenance.json). These are not measurements of the current intrapersonal roles.')
h('New measurements of reference, expression and interaction')
para('The [grounded reference and full-field study](../community-reference-field/README.md) adds a new public source with actual wording, object references, message times and independent human interpretations. Across 5,045 changed-wording pairs referring to the same object set, later interpretation agreement rises by 1.00 percentage point [0.19, 1.85]; this is an association, and identical reference is narrower than identical meaning. The coupled corpus equations were tested on 64 reserved scenario episodes under an explicit reference-field mapping, selected using 64 separate training scenarios. Spatial MSE is 11.771 versus 12.913 for the last observed field, but the paired uncertainty includes no advantage. Turning off the added force gives 11.775, and turning off the accumulated source gives 11.770. The distinctive mechanisms have not demonstrated a predictive benefit here. These errors have different units from the earlier correctness test.')
h('Full coupled field and the real-data test')
para('The [full coupled corpus-field test](../community-full-field/README.md) now runs momentum, pressure, incompressibility, signed-field transport and accumulated input together. Its explicitly proposed correctness mapping was tested on 455 later submissions in 127 evaluation groups, with fitting confined to separate training groups. Mean squared error is 0.1403 versus 0.1043 for retaining the last answer; 16 predictions fall outside [0,1]. The equations were retained, and the unsuccessful measurement link is reported. These are previously used public records, not untouched external validation. Different computed flows have identical total-field predictions, so this dataset cannot identify the spatial model. Intended meaning, treatment and penalty feedback still need their own measured links.')
h('Corrected corpus and real uptake records')
para('**Earlier community simulations included added equations.** The [corpus fidelity audit and real-record study](../community-mimesis/README.md) now uses the supplied corrected corpus explicitly. It preserves accumulated input A and source J=κA, all three threshold laws, exact-edge eligibility and the other stated mathematical relations. Logistic decisions and decaying penalty memory remain separately assumed extensions. Thirty-seven unit tests and 87 saved-result checks pass; this does not fit continuum social dynamics to text.')
para('In 162 candidate answer-uptake changes, 62 become correct, eight become incorrect and 92 remain incorrect. In 2,259 matched forum pairs, early unquoted phrase reuse differs by +2.30 percentage points between later attack-removal and control branches, with a 95% interval from −0.49 to +5.16. Repeated words often rebut or quote another person. [The full review](../community-mimesis/results/functional_audit.json) distinguishes acceptance, joint construction and mirrored challenge without claiming a causal imitation law.')
h('Current roles within one person')
para('Smoke and Clay are inward speaking and listening, affecting the moving idea in its Water, Fog, Mist, Wind and other forms. Each function can draw on different parts of that person’s remembered history. Water is perceived balance; perceived balance, calm, agreement and unresolved tension must be recorded separately. D₂O asks how a small compositional change can have a large consequence. No role is a diagnosis or fixed identity.')
para('**Keep strong language and state the missing comparison.** Coercion, resistance, pressure, refusal and boundaries remain available where they express the reported experience. The [current testing document](../community-two-in-one/report.html) separates definitions, measured findings and untested mechanisms.')
h('Earlier framework for external encounters')
h('Meaning, expression, context, treatment and memory')
para('**Follow the encounter:** stated meaning → expression in context → treatment → remembered consequences → a later encounter. Context also shapes which expressions are available. This is a proposed way to examine a community, with evidence attached to each connection. This older sequence concerns external encounters; the current inward Smoke and Clay mapping is defined above and is not validated by these external records.')
table(['Part','What to preserve'],[
 ['Meaning · Sens','The person’s account of what they mean; keep the receiver’s interpretation separate'],
 ['Expression · Sin','Exact words, actions or silence, with timing and register'],
 ['Context · c','Audience, rules, policy version, resources and relevant history, declared before comparing outcomes'],
 ['Treatment','What happens to the person: decision, reasons, severity, duration, work and help'],
 ['Memory','Whose experience, expectation or institutional record persists, and how it affects a later encounter']])
table(['Connection','Support now','Missing test'],[
 ['Meaning and expression within context','Described in the supplied diagrams','Check the speaker’s meaning and receiver’s interpretation in comparable episodes'],
 ['Rules and priorities → allocation','Tested under the fictional allocation rules below','Check whether those rules describe an observed community'],
 ['Past contributions → later requests','Tested in the linked adaptable-role model','Test the expectation update against new time-ordered observations'],
 ['Wording or prior treatment → later treatment in people','Real annotations, randomized recognition and observed penalty escalation, with distinct limits','Meaning-equivalent moderation contrasts and comparable-conduct history tests']])
para('**A source-described relationship is not automatically an observed causal effect.** Solid arrows in the supplied diagram identify source descriptions; dashed arrows identify operational connections still to specify or test. In the existing adaptable-role model, the no-memory control freezes expectation weights but still allows learning through practice. It does not remove every consequence of history.')
para('**Keep the strong language and identify its evidence.** Record the action, attribute the account and state the missing comparison. The older screenshot totals 83; the supplied corrected corpus reports 90 occurrences (70 body and 20 references). This update records that correction without independently rescanning the manuscript, and neither total alone establishes bias. Equal permit/restrict decisions also do not establish equal reasons, severity or fairness.')
para('The [full connections and evidence guide](CONNECTIONS.md) includes a worked fictional boundary example, the actual memory update, the Sens/Sin and Socio-Didact links, definitions of U, Ω and W, the distinction between score clearance and distance, and the tests still needed for field-to-decision mappings. Its initial conceptual addition was followed by the synthetic encounter tests below; no newly collected human observations are claimed.')
h('Completed checks against real data')
para('The [actual-moderation extension](https://github.com/NousVolition/Nous-Volition/blob/main/studies/community-moderation/README.md) checks real Reddit removals and Wikipedia block records. Among 8,687 accounts with two finite assigned blocks in the specified follow-up, 7,109 (81.8%) had a longer second assignment; medians rose from 24 to 72 hours. This documents escalation among accounts blocked again, not a causal effect of remembered history on the same later conduct.')
para('For wording, all 12 closest same-topic Reddit pairs reviewed changed substantive content, so they do not establish a wording-only effect. The separate Reddit penalty-history release lacks most subsequent outcomes: none of 1,914 matched comparisons has all four outcomes after joins. The [report and methods](https://github.com/NousVolition/Nous-Volition/blob/main/studies/community-moderation/METHODS.md) preserve these gaps and the strong language of criticism, refusal and resistance.')
para('The [real-data extension](https://github.com/NousVolition/Nous-Volition/blob/main/studies/community-real-data/README.md) checks 30,072 changed wording pairs with human content labels. Of these, 4,544 failed the content-match check. A single-assistant review found further substantive changes in 9 of 24 accepted pairs and uncertainty in 3; this is an audit requiring human review, not independent validation.')
para('Among 941 selected matched pairs with both offensiveness labels, 754 changed from offensive to nonoffensive and 3 in the reverse direction. Those are annotation judgments, not recorded penalties. In a separate randomized Wikipedia experiment, 12/100 initially awarded contributors received another award versus 2/100 controls: +10 percentage points, with a 95% interval of +2.9 to +17.9. This supports an effect of prior recognition in that setting; it does not identify a universal memory mechanism. [Evidence boundaries and reproducible analysis](https://github.com/NousVolition/Nous-Volition/blob/main/studies/community-real-data/METHODS.md).')
para('**Preserve the point as well as the force.** A rewrite can remove an accusation, change a target or weaken a refusal. A preferred wording is not automatically equivalent, and an offensiveness label does not decide truth or deserved treatment. Water, fog, smoke and clay remain changeable situational descriptions.')
h('Completed wording and prior-treatment tests')
para('The [new encounter study](https://github.com/NousVolition/Nous-Volition/blob/main/studies/community-encounters/README.md) adds 432 wording cases, 6,000 paired history paths and explicit controls. In its synthetic rule, a chosen wording penalty produces a 25.4-percentage-point average restriction-probability difference for the same authored offer; reversing the penalty reverses that difference. Wording-blind rules give zero difference. The texts preserve task and time limits, but complete meaning equivalence has not been independently assessed.')
para('One prior restriction changes the next 30 encounters’ restriction rate by +1.28 points under reinforcing feedback and −0.62 under a corrective rule. History-blind controls give zero difference; resetting both records removes later differences. These are consequences of specified rules, not measured family effects. Published wording and comment-rating summaries are checked separately, with two inconsistent wording estimates excluded. [Methods and evidence limits](https://github.com/NousVolition/Nous-Volition/blob/main/studies/community-encounters/METHODS.md).')
h('What was actually tested in the allocation benchmark')
para('768 main allocation cases cross 24 seeds, two skill patterns, two demand levels and eight organizational rules. Another 576 cases vary who receives priority, how strong it is and how much time assessment consumes. There are 36 tighter-tolerance pairs and 19 passing unit tests. These are optimization cases, not observed families or simulated conversations. Every arrangement uses the same ideal solver with complete information; distributed negotiation is not modeled.')
table(['Choice','What changes'],[
 ['Independent','Each person must supply their own two services'],
 ['Connected, total-focused','Help can cross nine bidirectional ties; requested time limits remain'],
 ['Partitioned','The same number of ties forms disconnected groups of three and four'],
 ['One member has priority','That member receives triple weight in the allocation objective'],
 ['Requests can be exceeded','The optimizer may use more time than members requested, within finite capacity'],
 ['Priority + overrides','Unequal priority and relaxed requested limits together'],
 ['Recording only','Metadata are recorded but do not alter allocation rules'],
 ['Assessment time cost','An assumed 0.1 time unit per member is consumed; no information benefit is modeled']])
para('Names are independent of abilities. Changing the seven labels leaves results exactly unchanged. Both graph types have nine undirected edges, but their degree sequences differ. A family-specific memory role for Clay or a contact style for Mist would require additional stated rules; those dynamics are not implied by the names.')
h('Results: the group total and the least-served member can move in opposite directions')
para('The table below uses the differentiated-skill, higher-demand setting and the 12 independent replication seeds. Each person has one total available-time unit and requests a work limit between 0.5 and 0.8. A needs score is the fraction of both abstract services received, not a wellbeing score. Full discovery and replication results for every setting are in [summary.csv](data/summary.csv) and [paired_contrasts.csv](data/paired_contrasts.csv).')
table(['Arrangement','Mean needs met','Mean of least-served score','Time beyond requests, total'],[
 [NAMES[k],f'{percent(k):.1f}%',f'{percent(k,"minimum_needs_met"):.1f}%',f'{p[k]["total_excess_over_requests"]["mean"]:.3f}'] for k in NAMES])
fig('outcomes','Bars show means; dots show the 12 seed outcomes. The lowest member score is retained separately from the group average.')
gain=percent('reciprocal')-percent('independent')
para(f'Connected allocation raises mean needs met from **{percent("independent"):.1f}% to {percent("reciprocal"):.1f}%**, a gain of {gain:.1f} percentage points (paired 95% seed-t interval 24.5–36.8 points). Yet the mean lowest-member score falls from **{percent("independent","minimum_needs_met"):.1f}% to {percent("reciprocal","minimum_needs_met"):.1f}%**. The objective maximizes total fulfillment and has no individual minimum guarantee. More available help does not force the optimizer to share its gains equally.')
para('The direction of the optimized total gain is guaranteed when the connected arrangement includes every independent option. The amount of the gain and its distribution are the numerical findings. Holding each person’s arithmetic mean skill fixed, the corresponding higher-demand coordination gain is only 2.2 percentage points when their two skills are equal. This supports a complementarity mechanism within this model, not a general law about personality types.')
para('Partitioning changes mean fulfillment by −2.9 percentage points relative to the connected graph; the paired seed interval is −8.3 to +2.4 points. This finite sample does not establish a consistent direction. Keeping the tie count equal prevents explaining the comparison solely by “more relationships,” but does not control every graph property.')
h('Who receives the benefit?')
fig('members','One illustrative community, the first replication seed. The priority position is arbitrary. A work/request ratio above 1 means the chosen allocation exceeds that member’s requested time; zero fulfillment displayed here is not a property of the Clay label.')
para(f'With member 0 given triple priority, that member’s mean fulfillment rises from {percent("reciprocal","leader_needs_met"):.1f}% to {percent("priority_hierarchy","leader_needs_met"):.1f}%, while the other six fall from {percent("reciprocal","others_needs_met"):.1f}% to {percent("priority_hierarchy","others_needs_met"):.1f}%. The group average barely changes. Moving priority through all seven positions gives an average recipient gain of **{100*s["rotated_priority_leader_gain"]["mean"]:.1f} percentage points** and a **{100*s["rotated_priority_others_change"]["mean"]:.1f}-point** change among the others, averaging within seed before calculating intervals.')
para(f'Allowing work beyond requested limits raises average fulfillment to {percent("override_budgets"):.1f}%, but uses **{p["override_budgets"]["total_excess_over_requests"]["mean"]:.2f} extra time units across seven people** beyond their requests. Relaxing a constraint can only improve this optimized objective. That is not evidence that overrides improve consent, wellbeing or family relationships; these are not modeled.')
fig('sensitivity','Priority and assessment-cost sensitivities. The intervals describe synthetic seed variation; untransformed interval bounds can extend beyond the metric range.')
para('Recording alone changes nothing exactly, because the model gives it no causal effect. Assessment that only consumes time reduces available work by construction. Measuring a real benefit of information would require imperfect knowledge, an explicit observation process and a rule for how information changes decisions. No claim that all assessment is harmful follows from these scenarios.')
h('What the passage adds to your project')
para('It adds a question about power inside the arrangement: who sets the objective, who has access to whom, whose needs receive priority and whose time counts as available? Your community can contain different members without treating one material name as superior. The model makes it possible to inspect both collective capacity and individual outcomes instead of using output alone as success.')
para('The earlier [family/community guide](https://github.com/NousVolition/Nous-Volition/blob/main/studies/substance-interactions/followup_tests/COMMUNITY.md), [SIMS model](https://github.com/NousVolition/Nous-Volition/tree/main/studies/social-organization) and [shared-rhythm study](https://github.com/NousVolition/Nous-Volition/tree/main/studies/sims-recovery-entrainment) remain separate, linked components. The substance study supplies physically tested transport mechanisms; this passage supplies a conceptual basis for organizational comparisons. No chemical kinetics or droplet forces were changed.')
para('A minimum-service guarantee, negotiation, fatigue, memory, changing relationships and a benefit from better information remain possible extensions. They were not silently added. No human participants, real family data or empirical validation of Foucault’s wider argument are involved.')
h('Reproduce and inspect')
para(f'The completed ensemble ran in {ex["seconds"]:.1f} seconds on the recorded environment. Maximum allocation-constraint residual was {ex["max_constraint_residual"]:.2g}; tightening the objective tolerance changed a member’s fulfillment by at most {ex["max_refinement_member_difference"]:.2g}. Numerical units are defined in [methods.md](methods.md). [Per-person results](data/members.csv) preserve who contributes and who receives help.')
code('python -m pip install -r requirements.txt\npython test_model.py\npython verify.py\n\n# Preserve the delivered data while rerunning:\npython run_study.py --out reproduced\npython analyze.py --data reproduced --out reproduced-analysis\n\n# Rebuild the delivered report from delivered data:\npython build_report.py')
para('`data/protocol.json` records the design and source hashes. `data/allocations.npz` contains every main effort, service flow and needs fraction, with order in `data/case_order.json`. `verification.json` records saved-result checks and selected reruns; `manifest.json` records packaged hashes. The runner refuses to overwrite a previous protocol. Counts of repeated controls and refinement solves are explicit in [execution.json](data/execution.json).')
